The 6.12 kernel tree that USED to be here has been removed. Deliberately.

The board runs 7.1.10 and `make linux` builds ../linux-71-port/. This
submodule was the old 6.12 port, referenced by nothing in the build - and it
was a trap rather than a resource:

  * PPA CLUT work was once written into THIS tree instead of linux-71-port/.
    It compiled nowhere, the symbol was simply absent from System.map, and the
    ioctl returned EINVAL with no clue why. See memory/s31-wrong-kernel-tree.
  * When it was removed on 2026-09-08 it still held 15 modified files,
    including drivers/gpu/drm/espressif/esp32s31-ppa.{c,h} - the stranded
    remains of exactly that mistake, sitting here for over a week.

The stranded diff is kept at ../patches/attic/0000-stranded-in-the-6.12-submodule.patch
purely as a record. It is superseded: the live esp32s31-ppa.c is 136 kB
against the stranded 58 kB and contains that work plus everything since.

Two identically-named kernel trees, one of which is silently not built, is a
mistake waiting to be repeated. Now there are no sources here to edit by
accident. If 6.12 is ever needed again it is in this repo's git history:

    git log --all -- .gitmodules      # the URL and branch
    https://github.com/GrieferPig/linux-esp32-s31.git  v6.12-esp32-s31
